Purpose:
  Follow each native lip silhouette instead of painting a shared oval.
  Remove Aster's artificial dark mouth corner, define Rowan's eyelid folds,
  halve only Rowan's emotion exaggeration, and replace opaque mouth voids
  with actual transparency during speech and yawns.

Tasks:
  Fit symmetric rest-space lipstick guides with a Cupid's-bow central dip.
  Share the same mask between filled, edge and other presentation paths.
  Attach a bounded transparent aperture to native animated lip-rim vertices.
  Align idle mouth fields with the selected native mouth and preserve closure.
  Add Rowan-only eyelid relief and halve its post-fit emotional deltas.
  Show effective Rowan emotion settings and preserve neutral speech/audio.
  Qualify all six heads, speech, yawns, turns, blinking and resource ownership.
  Update the chapter, guide, living journal, tracking and owned continuity.
  Reopen only this session's Verona head after qualification, keeping settings.

Acceptance criteria:
  Default/custom lipstick follows symmetric native upper/lower borders.
  Aster has no separate artificial black cavity/corner paint.
  Open mouths reveal the background, not opaque black or interior patches.
  Rowan receives half the previous emotion delta for every expression;
  neutral speech and the other five models retain their prior gains.
  Rowan eyelids retain complete blink closure and reopening without eye glow.
  No new network/model, continuous RAF, per-frame topology generation,
  transcript persistence, sibling interruption or unapproved release.
  Owner's Aster=Female assignment is recorded; other genders stay unassigned.

